        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                "word": "exoplanète",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "56d0ec9e-35b2-4152-ae67-62b859c0929d",
                        "entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "exoplanètes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                        "entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Planète extrasolaire, c'est-à-dire située en dehors du système solaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Planétologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d07e7f9a-8cf6-4f6f-899e-da496d18d371",
                                "sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                                "text": "Sur une exoplanète, même avec les mêmes éléments de base, l’environnement (atmosphère, eau, température, etc.) diffère nécessairement de celui de notre planète."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deb1df9e-602d-4827-b02b-93ca5fc968d0",
                                "sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                                "text": "Avec aussi le choix récent de créer un Pôle de recherche national («PlanetS») sur les exoplanètes, la Suisse fortifie sa position dans ce domaine scientifique de pointe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44bd3a97-3b54-4d6b-acc4-bba6a066b331",
                                "sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                                "text": "La découverte de 51 Pegasi b est la première d’une longue série : en moins de vingt ans, on a détecté plus d’un millier d’autres exoplanètes. Les noms de Michel Mayor et Didier Queloz seront pour toujours associés à ce nouveau domaine de l’astronomie, l’exoplanétologie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "109c95f2-988c-4c29-8e7c-0e53191c51a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Exoplanet",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Exoplanet",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91e74483-3a74-319b-bd3d-1cb8fc164403",
                                        "entry_id": "25aaae4c-724e-32a0-a063-28dd9737c64d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ein Planet, der ein Zentralgestirn in einem fremden Planetensystem umkreist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ee0e232-ed45-46a6-8b2f-c2a9c3cb41ff",
                                                "sense_id": "91e74483-3a74-319b-bd3d-1cb8fc164403",
                                                "text": "Astronomen haben erstmals einen Planeten um einen anderen Stern identifiziert, dessen Atmosphäre mehr Kohlenstoff als Sauerstoff enthält. Damit eröffnet er eine ganz neue Klasse von Exoplaneten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "829c423d-9414-461f-a484-2b03e0fb6f21",
                                                "sense_id": "91e74483-3a74-319b-bd3d-1cb8fc164403",
                                                "text": "Zum anderen aber bedeutet dies, dass auch andere, erdähnlichere Exoplaneten, eine kohlenstoffhaltige Atmosphäre und auch eine kohlenstoffhaltige Oberfläche besitzen könnten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25088802-d65c-4fcc-a642-3956e50bb8c4",
                                                "sense_id": "91e74483-3a74-319b-bd3d-1cb8fc164403",
                                                "text": "Ein Sternensystem allerdings, in dem einigermaßen vielversprechende Exoplaneten unterwegs sind, ist Gliese 581."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ae8ceeb-4f5c-4cba-b9f1-bbd110e50d36",
                                                "sense_id": "91e74483-3a74-319b-bd3d-1cb8fc164403",
                                                "text": "Immigration gibt es auch im Weltall: Ein internationales Team von Astronomen hat in der Milchstraße erstmals einen Exoplaneten mit extragalaktischem Ursprung entdeckt."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67d2e6fd-42ba-4f38-acba-a9cbbf36f71b",
                        "source_entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
                        "target_lang_word": "exoplanet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exoplanet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                        "entry_id": "d728d4e0-450b-33fb-a4de-5a022e444681",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A planet which exists outside Earth's solar system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba735412-930b-4591-850c-a03694bf2055",
                                                "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                                "text": "More such announcements will likely come in the months to follow, as the first space observatory dedicated to hunting exoplanets, called COROT, begins full operation and researchers complete their calculations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10527a9c-b765-420f-83c5-ea1999c7ca74",
                                                "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                                "text": "In the past two years, NASA’s Kepler Space Telescope has located nearly 3,000 exoplanet candidates ranging from sub-Earth-sized minions to gas giants that dwarf our own Jupiter. Their densities range from that of styrofoam to iron."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "512e12cf-a8bd-43b2-9f35-f387ec27683a",
                                                "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                                "text": "In a first for astronomers studying worlds beyond our solar system, data from the Hubble Space Telescope have revealed water vapor in the atmosphere of an Earth-size planet. Although this exoplanet orbits a star that is smaller than our sun, it falls within what’s known as the star’s habitable zone, the range of orbital distances where it would be warm enough for liquid water to exist on a planet’s surface."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5095e81c-999c-4854-8572-12033ca7e7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                                "text": "Astronomers have used two different exoplanet-detecting satellites to solve a cosmic mystery and reveal a rare family of six planets located about 100 light-years from Earth. […] Many exoplanets have been found orbiting dwarf stars that are much cooler and smaller than our sun, such as the famed TRAPPIST-1 system and its seven planets, announced in 2017."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d14d14b-3632-41f5-9566-ca61356f476e",
                                                "sense_id": "48d77ce3-a208-3bc8-b98e-a23b142a0fda",
                                                "text": "Now a team of researchers is offering what it contends is the strongest indication yet of extraterrestrial life, not in our solar system but on a massive planet, known as K2-18b, that orbits a star 120 light-years from Earth. A repeated analysis of the exoplanet’s atmosphere suggests an abundance of a molecule that on Earth has only one known source: living organisms such as marine algae."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e887f1a4-862b-4a0b-92ef-4897653b5ad9",
                        "source_entry_id": "533618c3-6508-3ebb-ae6d-3f0802cd1c4b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c03e7c10-a18a-36bf-a23e-a7afb48f156d",
